{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'))\nfor k in ['capacity','pending_work','candidates']: print(k,json.dumps(r.get(k),indent=2))\nPY\ncat storage_view_plan.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"description\": \"Fixed check for C_ACCEPTED_LOG_VIEW. Five-node producer prefix: leader 1 in term 2 creates an uncommitted entry replicated to node 2; leader 3 in term 3 installs a conflicting suffix at node 2 while winning votes from 4 and 5; leader 1 returns in term 4 using 4 and 5 and actual append retry restores its retained entry at node 2. Delay local completions FIFO, persist the intervening version, and hold latest replacement writes. Capture the expected full entry from emitted replacement work, admit the old completion, and compare the post-completion logical query. Then consume later completions, finish current writes, record the permitted stable-view control, and drain the network. Earlier explorations guide construction only; this check executes fresh.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"C_ACCEPTED_LOG_VIEW\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"source\": \"\",\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"description\": \"Serialized five-RawNode network and ordered MemoryStorage workers. Full actual producer history from a documented common snapshot prefix; internal state is observed without mutation.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"Substitute MemoryStorage for durable device I/O under a no-crash model.\",\n      \"Use a deterministic network scheduler with finite message loss and independent response recipient delays.\",\n      \"Read private logical log and unstable state for observations; no target code or dependencies are replaced.\",\n      \"Canonicalize actual entry contents as JSON strings for scalar comparison; this is reversible serialization, not hashing.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"replacement\",\n        \"event\": \"replacement\",\n        \"conditions\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admission\",\n        \"event\": \"old_completion_admitted\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"replacement_serial\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"reference\": \"replacement.serial\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"completion_type\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": \"MsgStorageAppendResp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"stale_response\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"stored_conflicts\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"pending_writes\",\n            \"op\": \"ne\",\n            \"value\": 0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src_async_delivery\",\n        \"src_async_config\",\n        \"src_raw_entry\",\n        \"src_startup\",\n        \"src_storage_contract\",\n        \"src_memory_storage\",\n        \"src_election\",\n        \"src_transfer_roles\",\n        \"src_replication\",\n        \"src_replication_retry\",\n        \"src_progress_reject\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"src_async_delivery\",\n        \"src_storage_contract\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"Use public RawNode Campaign, Propose, Ready, Step and Tick. Initialize five instances through MemoryStorage snapshot index/term 1, shared voters 1..5, HardState term/commit 1 and Applied 1, per the documented storage-backed bootstrap/restart interface. The driver runs actual election, append, rejection and retry producers; network policy loses finite packets to shape three terms. Append workers write entries and HardState in FIFO request order. Responses to node 2 are delayed FIFO after completed writes, while responses to remote recipients can progress. Later replacement writes to node 2 are delayed FIFO, then drained. No consensus state fields are assigned by the driver; private fields and log query methods are read only. MemoryStorage replaces durable device I/O without crash, so this does not test device durability.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"AsyncStorageWrites=true, fixed five-voter configuration, no crash, compaction, snapshot or configuration change inside the controlled interval. Every local response is produced by target code and delivered only after its request writes. Serialized execution supplies RawNode ownership. Two final ticks prompt retransmission; finite driver drain bound is a tool bound, not a liveness oracle.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"The synchronous interface has distinct documentation wording; it is excluded rather than borrowed for asynchronous permissions.\",\n        \"A disk-backed harness could test crash behavior, but that is outside this property and unnecessary for the logical overlay consumer.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M_STORAGE_VIEW\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"P_STORAGE_VIEW\",\n      \"event\": \"old_completion_result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"src_step\",\n          \"src_log_term_view\",\n          \"src_log_slice_view\",\n          \"src_unstable_stable\",\n          \"src_raw_append\",\n          \"src_unstable_replace\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"src_unstable_view_contract\",\n          \"src_storage_completion_contract\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"C_ACCEPTED_LOG_VIEW fixes preservation of accepted history during storage completion. The replacement prerequisite records canonical entry contents directly from the actual emitted MsgStorageAppend request after accepted follower replication. The result independently reads raftLog.slice after RawNode.Step returns from consuming the earlier completion. Comparison covers Index, Term, Type and Data in deterministic JSON, with no hash or inferred expected observation. This consumer-level assertion permits alternate correct storage strategies: it does not assert an unstable offset or require that every delayed message be ignored.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Admission requires an earlier captured replacement, a real MsgStorageAppendResp from a prior raft term, a conflicting stored entry and a pending replacement write. No history-changing call occurs between admission and the result query. Operation identity is op/node/entry_index, independent of the compared entry contents and changing term.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"Observed unstable offset and term fields diagnose protections but are not property predicates.\",\n          \"Current replacement completion is a permitted control recorded after the safety interval; eventual cluster agreement is not inferred from it.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"P_STORAGE_VIEW\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"phase\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"after_old_completion\"\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"log_entry\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"reference\": \"replacement.expected_entry\"\n      },\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op\",\n        \"node\",\n        \"entry_index\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"For the admitted delayed append completion, the logical entry returned after completion processing equals the independently captured current accepted replacement entry.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Bounded single producer history; no universal safety or crash-durability conclusion.\",\n    \"The final permitted completion and drain are diagnostics, not additional independent properties or consensus agreement evidence.\"\n  ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
